# .ignore.specs.yaml — marker file declaring spec coverage for the folder
# it sits in (and every subfolder, until a deeper marker overrides).
#
# Two valid contents:
#
# 1. EMPTY (or whitespace-only / comments-only): the folder is
#    deliberately exempt from spec coverage. Use for true cross-cutting
#    code that has no single owning feature (e.g., shared lib utilities).
#
# 2. ONE field naming a parent feature:
#
#      feature_name: <parent-feature-name>
#
#    The named feature MUST exist as some other folder's
#    __specs__/spec.yaml.feature_name. Use this when a folder's code is
#    logically owned by another feature whose spec lives elsewhere (a
#    route handler whose contract is documented in a feature folder, a
#    server-only adapter consumed by one feature, etc.).
#
# Inheritance: a deeper .ignore.specs.yaml overrides shallower; the
# closest marker (__specs__ OR .ignore) walked up from a source file
# wins.

feature_name: <parent-feature-name>
